<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report in Table <a href="#A7.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ G.1 Per-Category Results for 𝖬𝖱_𝖨𝗇𝗍𝗋𝖺 and 𝖬𝖱_𝖨𝗇𝗍𝖾𝗋 ‣ Appendix G Detailed Results ‣ Exploring Cross-Client Memorization of Training Data in Large Language Models for Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\sf MR_{Intra}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖬𝖱</mi><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗍𝗋𝖺</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\sf MR_{Intra}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\sf MR_{Inter}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖬𝖱</mi><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\sf MR_{Inter}}</annotation></semantics></math> results for each individual category of PAN2014 when used as the discriminator <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sf{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sf{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This provides the breakdown results from our main table (Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1 Memorization in Federated Learning ‣ 4 Results ‣ Exploring Cross-Client Memorization of Training Data in Large Language Models for Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
The results show that <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\sf MR_{Intra}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖬𝖱</mi><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗍𝗋𝖺</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\sf MR_{Intra}}</annotation></semantics></math> is higher than <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\sf MR_{Inter}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖬𝖱</mi><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗍𝖾𝗋</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\sf MR_{Inter}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for most categories.</p>
</div>
</section>
