<div id="A7.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#A7.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ G.6 Memorization with various Model Size ‣ Appendix G Detailed Results ‣ Exploring Cross-Client Memorization of Training Data in Large Language Models for Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>,
we observe no apparent impact of model sizes of both Qwen2.5-3B and Llama3.2-3B on any memorization types across tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.7 </span>Memorization with various Communication Rounds</h3>

<figure id="A7.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 14: </span>Impact of communication rounds(%)</figcaption>
<table id="A7.T14.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A7.T14.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T14.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Model</td>
<td id="A7.T14.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Tasks</td>
<td id="A7.T14.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A7.T14.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text"></span> <span id="A7.T14.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A7.T14.2.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="A7.T14.2.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
