<td id="A8.T16.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bbb" style="padding-left:3.1pt;padding-right:3.1pt;">37</td>
<td id="A8.T16.2.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bbb ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:3.1pt;padding-right:3.1pt;">2</td>
<td id="A8.T16.2.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bbb" style="padding-left:3.1pt;padding-right:3.1pt;">2</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The correlations between training input length, training output length, and generated suffix length (from our memorization framework) are shown in Table <a href="#A8.T16" title="Table 16 ‣ H.1 Correlations Between Input Length, Output Length, and Generated Suffix Length ‣ Appendix H Analysis ‣ Exploring Cross-Client Memorization of Training Data in Large Language Models for Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>.
We find that the generated suffix length is strongly affected by the input and output lengths.
Specifically, in summarization and classification tasks, the median of generated suffix lengths is close to the output length.
This phenomenon leads the classification task to generate a smaller token than other tasks to the point that its generated suffix length is smaller than the memorization threshold set in PAN2014, leading to 0.000% memorization in most of our experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.2 </span>Memorization Result of Incoherent Output Generation</h3>

<figure id="A8.T17" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 17: </span>Misclassify Memorization of Incoherent Output Generation</figcaption>
<table id="A8.T17.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A8.T17.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A8.T17.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:3.1pt;padding-right:3.1pt;">
<span id="A8.T17.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A8.T17.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Type</span>
</span></td>
