<div id="A8.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It is worth noting from Table <a href="#A8.T18" title="Table 18 ‣ H.3 Effects of Suffix Index ‣ Appendix H Analysis ‣ Exploring Cross-Client Memorization of Training Data in Large Language Models for Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> that memorization is more likely when the prefix and suffix are from the same client. Surprisingly, suffixes from group3 of Dialog task are memorized more than those from other clients. This suggests that the characteristic of a dataset to which suffixes belong plays an important role in their chance of being memorized.</p>
</div>
</section>
